1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,735
See this glowing dot?

2
00:00:01,735 --> 00:00:03,560
That's the whole universe.

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,400
Let me show you why.

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,680
This is a black hole.

5
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,395
And this bright ring is hot gas,

6
00:00:09,395 --> 00:00:10,790
spinning around it.

7
00:00:11,125 --> 00:00:12,530
Let's look at it from above.

8
00:00:14,325 --> 00:00:15,185
See?

9
00:00:15,185 --> 00:00:17,180
The disk is actually flat.

10
00:00:17,255 --> 00:00:18,860
This is the back half.

11
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,620
And this is the front half.

12
00:00:20,915 --> 00:00:21,980
Now watch the back half,

13
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,490
as we go back down.

14
00:00:24,655 --> 00:00:26,020
The black hole bends its light,

15
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,846
up over the top...

16
00:00:28,846 --> 00:00:30,150
and under the bottom.

17
00:00:30,965 --> 00:00:33,060
Now let's fly in closer.

18
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,320
Much closer.

19
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,335
If you hover right here,

20
00:00:36,335 --> 00:00:37,220
the black hole fills

21
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:39,760
exactly half your sky.

22
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,515
And see this thin line?

23
00:00:41,515 --> 00:00:41,820
That's light,

24
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,665
going around the black hole in a circle.

25
00:00:44,665 --> 00:00:47,365
Light can go all the way around...

26
00:00:47,365 --> 00:00:48,620
and come back to you.

27
00:00:49,065 --> 00:00:50,060
So in this line,

28
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:52,420
you see the back of your own head.

29
00:00:53,015 --> 00:00:54,000
Now let's go lower,

30
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,560
and hover just above the edge.

31
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,510
Then look up.

32
00:00:57,905 --> 00:00:59,240
The whole universe shrinks

33
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:02,210
into one small dot above you.

34
00:01:02,935 --> 00:01:03,790
And down here,

35
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:05,270
time runs slower.

36
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,230
Stay for one minute...

37
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:09,710
and half an hour goes by out there.

38
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:12,305
And all this darkness around the dot?

39
00:01:12,305 --> 00:01:13,690
That's the black hole.
